cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Feedback Suppression of Adaptation in AI-Written Structured State"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible research framework and controlled study of the feedback that
  arises when AI-generated typed structured state becomes machine-readable
  evidence for subsequent automated decisions, under fixed decision policies with
  no parameter updates or retraining. Separates behavioural producer deference
  from architectural readable write-back, reports a negative provenance result,
  and includes a UCI-derived external-validity boundary analysis.
